WEBVTT

01-01
00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:01.993
Welcome to session three.

01-02
00:00:02.173 --> 00:00:07.720
This week we connect two questions that arise whenever we use an
activity model.

01-03
00:00:07.900 --> 00:00:14.087
First, do the data satisfy the thermodynamic relationships that a
mixture must obey?

01-04
00:00:14.267 --> 00:00:22.763
Second, does the predicted liquid remain as one phase, or can it lower
its Gibbs energy by separating into two liquids?

01-05
00:00:22.943 --> 00:00:26.890
We will address consistency before liquid stability.

01-06
00:00:27.070 --> 00:00:37.019
That order matters: a convincing fit does not, by itself, establish
either consistency of the measurements or stability of the predicted
state.

01-07
00:00:37.199 --> 00:00:40.697
Keep your calculations, predictions, and corrections.

01-08
00:00:40.877 --> 00:00:44.355
